+## pytest Marker Strategy (S4_3 SQA Decision)
+
+Markers control which workflow runs which tests:
+
+| Marker | Tests Tagged | CI Workflow | When it Runs |
+|--------|-------------|-------------|--------------|
+| `ui` | Playwright browser tests | `playwright.yml` | PR to main + manual |
+
+`python-app.yml` runs `pytest -m "not ui"` so browser tests never slow the main check. More markers follow the same pattern as new test types arrive in later sprints.
+
+Markers defined in: `pyproject.toml` → `[tool.pytest.ini_options]` → `markers`
+
+## User Journey as Test Specification
+
+The S4_2 user journey document served as the specification for S4_3 Playwright tests.
+Each journey step maps directly to a Playwright action. If the journey is well written,
+the test writes itself. If the test is hard to write, the journey was incomplete.
